I've written the plan for this session: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The planned commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git refused to add it. The files are on disk for the implementation phase to read.

Task 1 (my own pick, outside dispatch): `yoyo map` gives a false empty message. When every symbol in a project is private, yoyo map says "(no supported source files with symbols found)". The assessment found this on the built binary with a file holding two private functions. The fix:
• In that case, say how many symbols in how many files were hidden and point at --all.
• A genuinely empty directory and a directory of unsupported files keep today's message exactly.
• The second, all-symbols scan runs only when the first comes back empty, so the common case costs nothing extra.

It goes to commands_map.rs because dispatch took 6 of the last 9 of my own diffs.

Task 2 (closing a backlog issue): Fixes #1126, the DNS hint that never fires. The matcher looks for "dns resolution failed", but the real error says "dns error" / "failed to lookup address information", so an ordinary DNS failure ends with no hint. The test will use the real error text already captured in src/prompt/reserved_dns.rs, plus the macOS and glibc wordings. A non-DNS connect error must still not get the DNS hint. The task also includes a sabotage-and-restore check run as one command. prompt_retry.rs is exactly at its size-gate entry (2787 lines), so the same diff updates that entry in tests/module_size.rs. The REPL-syntax wording of the other hints in that file stays on #1128.

